  "findings": [
    "Locally authored R2000 DXF seeds set ACAD group 1003 to PROBE_LAYER on the NOD and ACAD_MLINESTYLE owner. ODA File Converter created AC1012 and AC1014 DWGs, then reopened each into AC1027 DXF; ezdxf found PROBE_LAYER in both selected dictionaries.",
    "A separate bit walker binds each source dictionary frame, size, CRC, own handle, APPID, EED bytes, body boundary, entry names, owner, hard-owner extension handle and item roles. Both selected records reference layer 0x2f in big-endian EED. The source extension dictionary frames are independently walked with exact owner, one membership and item role.",
    "LibreDWG identifies each extension child as an XRECORD owned by its extension dictionary, with a matching reactor and the recorded EXTNAMES values. This is a peer-model observation; its physical XRECORD body is not independently bound by this control.",
    "The selected R14 parent dictionaries contain byte 0; their extension dictionaries contain byte 1. LibreDWG interprets the latter as is_hardowner=1, while the ODA document labels this field unknown. The observation does not establish native ownership semantics or justify broadening the zero-byte observer.",
    "On this generated source, strict and partial AC1012 conversion preserve the destination and stop at the cross-version ModelDocViewStyle guard. Strict AC1014 stops at complete-read disposition; explicit partial AC1014 stops at the LAYOUT/BLOCK_RECORD backlink guard. These are distinct from, and precede, output qualification of the selected extension graphs."
  ],
  "nextActions": [
    "Bind each extension XRECORD physical body, class identity, string encodings, owner/reactor roles and following-frame boundary; verify the source extension graph against more than one producer state.",
    "Establish the R14 byte meaning and versioned DXF projection using version-qualified authority or an independent native semantic witness. Then implement bounded source and staged-output graph closure with nondefault layer identity, both encodings, wrong-role/ambiguous/missing-target refusal and same-adapter retry.",
    "Resolve the separate whole-file disposition and backlink guards before claiming whole-source conversion. Keep unqualified extension data raw or refuse output."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "ODA-generated controls are not native AutoCAD producer or duplicate/merge evidence. LibreDWG XRECORD values are not an independent physical-body proof.",
    "The two source frames were created locally from scratch and no DWG/DXF fixture is committed."
  ],
